    "description": "Hemingray Glass Insulators Lot - 3 Pieces\nHemingray Glass Company, No. 17 and Patent 1893 Models\nAqua Blue and Clear, Vintage 19th to 20th Century\nThis collection features three vintage glass insulators produced by the Hemingray Glass Company, once the world's largest manufacturer of glass insulators. These utilitarian pieces were originally designed to support telegraph and telephone wires, and are now highly sought after for their iconic industrial aesthetic and diverse color variations.\nPieces Included:\nInsulator, Aqua Blue glass, marked \"HEMINGRAY\" and \"PATENT MAY 2 1893,\" featuring sharp drip points on the base edge.\nInsulator, Clear glass, marked \"HEMINGRAY-17,\" featuring a smooth flared base with a textured grip ring.\nInsulator, Clear glass, marked \"HEMINGRAY-17,\" featuring a smooth flared base with a textured grip ring.\nCondition:\nThe aqua blue insulator shows significant internal soot or carbon deposits and surface grime from authentic outdoor service. The clear insulators show minor surface wear and occasional internal bubbles characteristic of molded utility glass. No significant structural cracks are observed, though minor fleabites consistent with industrial usage may be present along the base edges.\nTHANK YOU FOR YOUR PURCHASE!\nIf you’re happy and you know it, please leave a 5-star rating! If there is a problem with your order, please contact us via Shop Goodwill before opening returns/claims. We strive to return all messages within one business day.\nPlease click the shipping estimate link in the listing to get the shipping costs directly from FedEx.  There will be no discounts or price changes after an auction has ended.\nOur shipping team works hard to get out all orders as quickly as possible, that being said it may take up to 5 business days after payment for your order to ship out.  Once it ships out you will receive tracking information.\n***IMPORTANT*** If your item was damaged in transit, do not throw away anything, including the box or packing materials until we have authorized you to do so. Photos will be required to file insurance claims.\nOur Business hours: Monday - Friday  8:00 am to 4:00 pm Central\nNew items and unique treasures are added daily, come back soon!",
